{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A burnt-offering.</b> He shall burn it under the name of an olah-offering." "<b>A fire-offering.</b> When he slaughters it, his slaughter must be for the name of the fire; and every אִשֶּׁה is a term of fire; פוש\"ייר בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>A pleasing fragrance.</b> Contentment before Me — for I spoke and My will was done (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French *feu/foyer*, 'fire/hearth'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:37.284767007Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}